The process was fairly disorganised. I applied in January, but only heard back late February. I found a job in the meantime, but accepted the HR call out of curiosity. The (external) rep didn't have that much info on that position and we decided on me asking for a follow-up after I settle into my new position a bit more. That decision was ignored as, about 2 weeks later, I got an e-mail asking to schedule for the 3 technical-ish interviews. I was still curious what the position entailed, so we scheduled the interviews on 3 consecutive days. The first one went alright, I messed up the second one. The interviewers were pleasant and professional. However, the 3rd interviewer didn't show up. I gave up after waiting for about 20 minutes and sent an inquiry to the HR rep. I got an automated e-mail the next day that I had been rejected, but there was no feedback or anything. This level of disregard definitely left a sour taste in my mouth.
